He takes one tater tot and he smashes it in the bottom of each mini taco and then he'll put whatever your breakfast order is inside.

1258
00:56:38.150 --> 00:56:40.030
She said, it's genius.

1259
00:56:40.350 --> 00:56:41.370
Sign me up.

1260
00:56:41.490 --> 00:56:43.190
You had me at smash tater tot.

1261
00:56:43.490 --> 00:56:47.690
She said if he had a taco stand or a restaurant, I would go every day.

1262
00:56:48.190 --> 00:56:49.390
Oh, my gosh.

1263
00:56:49.610 --> 00:56:50.870
That sounds so good.

1264
00:56:51.290 --> 00:56:55.470
Well, you know, I was trading texts with Sergio about being on the podcaSt.

1265
00:56:55.950 --> 00:57:00.850
Talk about someone who responded right away with such enthusiasm, much like BJ.

1266
00:57:00.850 --> 00:57:03.790
He could not wait to talk to us.

1267
00:57:03.930 --> 00:57:09.110
He's such a lovely person and we had so much fun going down memory lane with him.

1268
00:57:09.270 --> 00:57:09.670
We did.

1269
00:57:09.910 --> 00:57:13.950
We Zoomed with him the other day and we can't wait for you to hear our chat with him.

1270
00:57:14.070 --> 00:57:16.070
So here is our chat with Sergio.

1271
00:57:19.270 --> 00:57:20.490
Hello, Sergio.

1272
00:57:21.030 --> 00:57:21.570
Hi there.

1273
00:57:21.810 --> 00:57:21.910
Hi, Louise.

1274
00:57:22.510 --> 00:57:23.030
Thanks.

1275
00:57:23.590 --> 00:57:25.330
Thank you for coming on the podcaSt.

1276
00:57:25.850 --> 00:57:28.050
I love the podcast, by the way.

1277
00:57:28.310 --> 00:57:31.210
You all have nice voices, so it's soothing to the ear.

1278
00:57:31.210 --> 00:57:34.170
Yeah, it's funny and it's a lot of fun.

1279
00:57:34.710 --> 00:57:35.750
Aw, thanks, Sergio.

1280
00:57:36.170 --> 00:57:39.770
It was so nice seeing you when we visited the paper.

1281
00:57:40.170 --> 00:57:40.650
I know.

1282
00:57:40.830 --> 00:57:41.350
I like that.

1283
00:57:41.530 --> 00:57:42.910
That was such a surprise.

1284
00:57:43.290 --> 00:57:47.790
We were slammed for breakfast, but it was nice seeing you guys.

1285
00:57:47.970 --> 00:57:56.090
And also being on that show, you know, kind of like, you know, having some of the crew members from the office and, you know, Oscar.

1286
00:57:56.550 --> 00:57:58.450
It was awesome doing that show, too.

1287
00:57:58.530 --> 00:58:00.730
It just brings a lot of memories.

1288
00:58:01.210 --> 00:58:03.130
Of what we had in the office, you know?

1289
00:58:03.390 --> 00:58:05.290
Well, Sergio, you are so loved.

1290
00:58:05.530 --> 00:58:11.050
I have noticed pretty much every time I'm on a set where Mindy's running the show, you're there.

1291
00:58:11.230 --> 00:58:15.450
Like, the office family loves you and they always want to work with you.

1292
00:58:15.770 --> 00:58:17.490
Yeah, no, I appreciate that.

1293
00:58:17.710 --> 00:58:23.630
It's been amazing being part of the office, you know, because we had a lot of great times, right?

1294
00:58:23.630 --> 00:58:25.950
It was such an amazing time.

1295
00:58:26.170 --> 00:58:31.050
And for me as a cook and cooking for y'all, it was special.

1296
00:58:31.510 --> 00:58:40.150
You know, you mentioned breakfast and Kelly shared with us that you have started doing mini tacos for breakfaSt.

1297
00:58:40.430 --> 00:58:47.330
She said you took her breakfast order and put it in a tiny taco and she said she can't get enough of it.

1298
00:58:47.330 --> 00:58:49.710
Yeah, Kelly, it was awesome working with Kelly.

1299
00:58:50.030 --> 00:58:53.750
And yeah, she has like little orders, small orders, kind of like Angela.

1300
00:58:54.190 --> 00:58:56.850
When Angela used to order her little Angela size.

1301
00:58:57.230 --> 00:58:58.150
Yeah, Angie size.

1302
00:58:58.570 --> 00:59:00.810
Yeah, that was fun.

1303
00:59:01.250 --> 00:59:05.230
So, Sergio, you have been in this food business for so long.

1304
00:59:05.390 --> 00:59:08.330
How do you keep coming up with new ideas and new recipes?

1305
00:59:08.330 --> 00:59:11.910
We're so curious how you put a menu together for the week.

1306
00:59:12.330 --> 00:59:18.270
Well, when I started the office, it was hard because there was no iPhone, right?

1307
00:59:18.450 --> 00:59:22.590
And I had to go through the cookbooks, you know, and just get the ideas from there.

1308
00:59:22.730 --> 00:59:26.290
And the feedback from the crew, that's kind of what you work with.

1309
00:59:26.430 --> 00:59:27.510
Like, oh, they like this.

1310
00:59:27.510 --> 00:59:30.090
So, you know, we're going that direction.

1311
00:59:30.290 --> 00:59:33.830
But yeah, it got easier when the iPhone came around, you know.

1312
00:59:34.010 --> 00:59:36.310
So it was just a lot easier.

1313
00:59:36.550 --> 00:59:40.670
But yeah, it was through crew members, what they like and all that.

1314
00:59:40.670 --> 00:59:46.730
So I have to ask you, you know, you're using word of mouth about what's a hit, what's not.

1315
00:59:47.250 --> 00:59:51.730
Was there a recipe you ever did that people were like, don't do that one again?

1316
00:59:52.110 --> 00:59:55.130
Or was there one where everyone was like, you have to do that one again?

1317
00:59:55.290 --> 00:59:58.030
Like, what are your hits and your misses?

1318
00:59:58.510 --> 01:00:01.570
They never really tell you like, oh, that wasn't good.

1319
01:00:01.770 --> 01:00:05.030
You know, I only got that once.

1320
01:00:05.190 --> 01:00:08.350
And that was the Teamsters in New York, you know, one time.

1321
01:00:08.350 --> 01:00:11.730
But only like as a family, like they already liked me a lot.

1322
01:00:12.010 --> 01:00:13.430
And they told me, hey, we love you.

1323
01:00:13.590 --> 01:00:18.270
But that last meal, you know, that's the only time they told me.

1324
01:00:18.510 --> 01:00:20.410
But it was the Teamsters in New York, you know.

1325
01:00:20.590 --> 01:00:25.210
But other than that, with the office and all that, everybody was so nice.

1326
01:00:25.410 --> 01:00:25.990
It was beautiful.

1327
01:00:26.590 --> 01:00:28.150
Well, your food is amazing.

1328
01:00:28.430 --> 01:00:31.230
That's why I couldn't believe anyone would ever tell you this was a miss.

1329
01:00:31.430 --> 01:00:35.490
But, you know, Jenna and I both had so many meals that we loved.

1330
01:00:35.490 --> 01:00:37.550
What was your most requested meal?

1331
01:00:38.270 --> 01:00:40.150
The most requested meal?

1332
01:00:40.430 --> 01:00:46.690
It's the action stations, you know, like the pasta bars, the taco bars.

1333
01:00:46.750 --> 01:00:50.310
The crew always loved that, the action stations.

1334
01:00:50.670 --> 01:00:59.150
So every time we had like a fun station and, you know, especially the pasta bar and the taco bar, those are always a hit.

1335
01:00:59.150 --> 01:01:01.690
Well, I remember your pasta bar.

1336
01:01:01.910 --> 01:01:02.750
I was a fan.

1337
01:01:03.210 --> 01:01:08.690
And you would have like all the different pastas and all the different ingredients and then different sauces.

1338
01:01:08.970 --> 01:01:11.510
And it was kind of like an omelet bar.

1339
01:01:11.670 --> 01:01:16.370
You just walk up and point to all the things you wanted and you guys would make it right there on the spot.

1340
01:01:16.590 --> 01:01:17.030
Yeah.

1341
01:01:17.210 --> 01:01:18.190
It was so great.

1342
01:01:18.470 --> 01:01:19.250
It was fun.

1343
01:01:19.470 --> 01:01:20.630
I tried and have it.

1344
01:01:20.630 --> 01:01:27.050
So when like also when Isabella, when she was young, she used to just eat plain pasta, right?

1345
01:01:27.350 --> 01:01:27.690
Yeah.

1346
01:01:28.010 --> 01:01:29.370
That was her go-to.

1347
01:01:29.670 --> 01:01:35.230
So, you know, it reminds me of that too, when Isabella was young coming to set.

1348
01:01:35.630 --> 01:01:37.310
You were so sweet with her.

1349
01:01:37.550 --> 01:01:41.350
You would always set aside a little buttered noodles dish for her.

1350
01:01:41.710 --> 01:01:44.710
You took such good care of all of us in that way.

1351
01:01:44.730 --> 01:01:45.070
Yeah.

1352
01:01:45.070 --> 01:01:50.210
You know, we grew into a family there and there's nothing like that, you know, ever going to happen again.

1353
01:01:50.350 --> 01:01:52.130
I don't think once in a lifetime.

1354
01:01:52.910 --> 01:02:02.970
Another thing, Sergio, is that you were able to like make a meal that was good for the people who were dairy-free and gluten-free and vegetarian.

1355
01:02:03.030 --> 01:02:07.190
And you would have a meat option, but then you would have also a fish option.

1356
01:02:07.430 --> 01:02:08.550
How do you do it?

1357
01:02:08.630 --> 01:02:14.110
And also at breakfast, I never heard anybody order breakfast and you didn't have whatever the thing was.

1358
01:02:14.110 --> 01:02:20.330
Like, this is a silly question, but where do you keep all this food and who does the grocery shopping?

1359
01:02:20.510 --> 01:02:21.470
How do you do this?

1360
01:02:21.910 --> 01:02:22.150
Yeah.

1361
01:02:22.390 --> 01:02:33.810
So, so when, when it started, you know, season one, um, the mise en place for breakfast was a little bit small, but as the show grew in the, into the years, you know,

1362
01:02:34.270 --> 01:02:38.130
like by the third season, you know, same crew members, the caSt.

1363
01:02:38.130 --> 01:02:42.510
And, and so everybody had their little, you know, little specialty.

1364
01:02:42.810 --> 01:02:52.530
So I had to make sure I had this, I had to make sure I had goat cheese because a couple of orders, you know, and it grew the mise en place for breakfaSt.

1365
01:02:52.850 --> 01:03:00.070
It grew like more and more as the years went on, but by the ninth season, I had a lot of stuff in the fridge.

1366
01:03:00.070 --> 01:03:02.790
But I bet, I bet you did.

1367
01:03:03.050 --> 01:03:09.670
I mean, I feel like there were people who were like, I want my breakfast order, but will you throw some like hot peppers on it today?

1368
01:03:09.870 --> 01:03:10.810
And you'd say, sure.

1369
01:03:11.230 --> 01:03:11.430
Yeah.

1370
01:03:11.970 --> 01:03:12.530
No, yeah.

1371
01:03:12.810 --> 01:03:15.490
Especially I had, I had the Rashida special.

1372
01:03:15.690 --> 01:03:16.910
That one was a hit, right?

1373
01:03:17.050 --> 01:03:18.210
Remember the Rashida special?

1374
01:03:18.830 --> 01:03:20.530
That one was such a hit.

1375
01:03:20.530 --> 01:03:22.090
So I had to have black beans.

1376
01:03:22.330 --> 01:03:29.830
I had to have, you know, turkey bacon every day, every day, you know, that because corn tortillas, the green salsa, you know.

1377
01:03:30.330 --> 01:03:31.790
Yeah, that one really took off.

1378
01:03:32.030 --> 01:03:33.010
Yeah, it took off.

1379
01:03:33.130 --> 01:03:35.970
That took off for a while too.

1380
01:03:36.470 --> 01:03:38.790
But, you know, Sergio, I was so curious.

1381
01:03:38.790 --> 01:03:40.510
I've always wanted to ask you this.

1382
01:03:40.590 --> 01:03:43.150
How did you start as a chef?

1383
01:03:43.350 --> 01:03:45.450
What was your journey to doing this?

1384
01:03:45.450 --> 01:03:51.930
So I started, you know, this catering company as a dishwasher at 18.

1385
01:03:52.510 --> 01:03:54.830
And then I moved up, moved up the ranks.

1386
01:03:55.030 --> 01:03:57.970
And then they gave me a shot, the catering company I was at.

1387
01:03:58.090 --> 01:04:01.730
They gave me a shot as a chef, kind of young, like at 24.

1388
01:04:01.810 --> 01:04:04.190
And I was like chef in commercials.

1389
01:04:04.450 --> 01:04:05.890
That's all I was doing.

1390
01:04:05.910 --> 01:04:08.470
So I had like five day recipes.

1391
01:04:08.470 --> 01:04:10.290
That's all I needed for commercials.

1392
01:04:10.890 --> 01:04:14.370
And so then I got the call to do the office.

1393
01:04:14.370 --> 01:04:20.890
So the office was my first show and like full on five days a week, months, you know.

1394
01:04:21.050 --> 01:04:22.450
So I was real nervous.

1395
01:04:22.770 --> 01:04:24.570
Like I was nervous on the first day.

1396
01:04:24.790 --> 01:04:29.150
And then the second day, the craft service, then it was another craft.

1397
01:04:29.250 --> 01:04:31.250
It wasn't it wasn't Peter and Rotten.

1398
01:04:31.470 --> 01:04:35.910
But that craft service told me on the second day, it said they were talking about you.

1399
01:04:36.190 --> 01:04:40.390
And I was like real horrified that they were like something.

1400
01:04:41.050 --> 01:04:43.190
Yeah, and it was good news, right?

1401
01:04:43.330 --> 01:04:45.070
He says they were talking good about your food.

1402
01:04:45.390 --> 01:04:48.610
And that gave me the confidence to try hard and all that.

1403
01:04:48.870 --> 01:04:51.450
And it was such a nice crew that it was easy to do.

1404
01:04:51.830 --> 01:04:55.710
But I learned a lot through the office, you know, through the casting crew.

1405
01:04:55.850 --> 01:05:01.410
I learned a lot like, you know, like through the cooking and took it, took it with me to the other shows.

1406
01:05:01.410 --> 01:05:03.950
But yeah, the office was my school.

1407
01:05:04.390 --> 01:05:08.130
How much did you coordinate with Michael and Vartan?

1408
01:05:08.310 --> 01:05:12.510
Because they would bring out like a certain hot snack every day at 10 o'clock.

1409
01:05:12.710 --> 01:05:14.250
And did you guys talk?

1410
01:05:14.430 --> 01:05:21.190
Like, were you sure to be like, OK, if they're doing a hot dog bar, I'm not going to do hot dogs at lunch?

1411
01:05:21.790 --> 01:05:22.690
We did.

1412
01:05:22.930 --> 01:05:23.430
We tried.

1413
01:05:23.570 --> 01:05:31.390
But for some reason, we still always ended up doing the same thing, you know, kind of, you know, like, oh, you're doing that?

1414
01:05:32.370 --> 01:05:33.470
So, but yeah.

1415
01:05:33.650 --> 01:05:34.230
Oh, that's so funny.

1416
01:05:34.450 --> 01:05:36.110
I don't have that memory at all.

1417
01:05:36.270 --> 01:05:41.290
I was like, somehow you guys never managed to double up in my mind.

1418
01:05:41.450 --> 01:05:42.390
OK, that's good.

1419
01:05:42.550 --> 01:05:46.470
Because, yeah, Peter and Vartan, you know, like we come up with something.

1420
01:05:46.630 --> 01:05:48.090
I'm doing that today.

1421
01:05:48.090 --> 01:05:52.790
But yeah, they were so much fun, those two guys, man.

1422
01:05:52.890 --> 01:05:53.870
I loved them.

1423
01:05:54.150 --> 01:05:55.250
And I miss them.

1424
01:05:55.870 --> 01:05:56.910
Yeah, same.

1425
01:05:57.310 --> 01:06:05.910
You know, Sergio, I'm so curious, too, because you are planning meals all the time and huge meals, too.

1426
01:06:06.290 --> 01:06:08.110
Do you plan any meals at home?

1427
01:06:08.270 --> 01:06:10.750
Are you just like once you're home, you are done meal planning?

1428
01:06:11.270 --> 01:06:12.070
No, I am.

1429
01:06:12.230 --> 01:06:12.750
I do.

1430
01:06:12.950 --> 01:06:16.230
I actually cook for my boys on the weekend.

1431
01:06:16.230 --> 01:06:18.510
I see them on the weekend.

1432
01:06:18.830 --> 01:06:21.110
So we do every weekend.

1433
01:06:21.290 --> 01:06:24.790
We I do a dinner and we watch movies.

1434
01:06:24.990 --> 01:06:27.530
And I like to cook here, too.

1435
01:06:27.790 --> 01:06:31.690
It's a lot funner and, you know, get to experience new stuff.

1436
01:06:31.830 --> 01:06:32.990
I like cooking at home.

1437
01:06:33.190 --> 01:06:34.430
It's that when I'm working.

1438
01:06:34.430 --> 01:06:39.170
If I'm working, then, you know, only that Saturday is the only day I'll cook.

1439
01:06:39.370 --> 01:06:40.430
Oh, that's fair.

1440
01:06:40.430 --> 01:06:47.470
Well, you know, I love your food so much that when I worked on the office,

1441
01:06:47.470 --> 01:06:53.610
I would go through the lunch line and I would pick something for lunch and then I would wait for everybody to eat.

1442
01:06:53.610 --> 01:07:03.930
And then as you all would start to kind of pack up stuff, like lunch was over, I would go through and I would get one of your to go containers and I would pick something.

1443
01:07:04.130 --> 01:07:05.610
And that's what I would eat for dinner.

1444
01:07:06.070 --> 01:07:07.510
Yeah, that's nice.

1445
01:07:07.690 --> 01:07:12.830
So I would eat your food twice a day for all those years on the office.

1446
01:07:13.330 --> 01:07:14.210
Thank you so much.

1447
01:07:14.310 --> 01:07:15.670
I appreciate that, Jenna.

1448
01:07:15.890 --> 01:07:16.230
Thank you.

1449
01:07:16.230 --> 01:07:20.650
Yeah, there was many times we were taking food home.

1450
01:07:20.950 --> 01:07:21.310
Oh, yeah.

1451
01:07:21.950 --> 01:07:27.150
Sergio, do you have a favorite food memory from the office or a behind the scenes memory?

1452
01:07:27.410 --> 01:07:30.310
It doesn't have to be food related just from your time on the show.

1453
01:07:31.430 --> 01:07:34.370
Yeah, it's my most memorable one.

1454
01:07:34.570 --> 01:07:42.930
It was kind of a sad one, but it was Steve Carell's last day and we went to the warehouse and we did that beautiful speech.

1455
01:07:42.930 --> 01:07:50.570
And then we took the time to talk to every department, you know, and I'll never forget it.

1456
01:07:50.710 --> 01:07:53.650
It's like, you know, there wasn't a dry eye in the room.

1457
01:07:53.830 --> 01:07:58.330
Everybody was, it was the most memorable one that I'll never forget.

1458
01:07:59.030 --> 01:07:59.230
Yeah.

1459
01:08:00.030 --> 01:08:03.270
Have you run into Steve since the office wrapped?

1460
01:08:03.550 --> 01:08:03.890
Yes.

1461
01:08:03.890 --> 01:08:17.430
Yeah, so when Vartan passed away, I found out, you know, about it through Debbie and me, Alan, and Debbie went and we were right there at the funeral.

1462
01:08:17.910 --> 01:08:22.850
And then it was, you know, us three and in walks Steve Carell.

1463
01:08:23.110 --> 01:08:26.710
And it was like, it was us four right there.

1464
01:08:26.850 --> 01:08:28.770
And that's, you know, that's a beautiful moment.

1465
01:08:29.490 --> 01:08:33.650
And we got to, you know, talk with Steve Carell about the office.

1466
01:08:34.070 --> 01:08:36.430
And that was the last time I saw him.

1467
01:08:36.790 --> 01:08:41.910
I also saw him on Space Force, but the last time was Vartan, I believe.

1468
01:08:42.450 --> 01:08:43.050
Yeah.

1469
01:08:43.270 --> 01:08:52.250
I know several people have always asked us about the different menus on the show and what our favorite meal was.

1470
01:08:52.250 --> 01:08:56.250
And, you know, Sergio, my favorite was anything with your salsa.

1471
01:08:56.530 --> 01:08:58.490
We've, I've talked about that a lot.

1472
01:08:58.870 --> 01:09:03.350
But, Sergio, do you actually have a favorite dish for yourself?

1473
01:09:03.590 --> 01:09:05.910
Like, what is your favorite go-to snack?

1474
01:09:06.190 --> 01:09:08.590
For a snack, I like the Chico stick.

1475
01:09:09.050 --> 01:09:09.730
Oh, yeah?

1476
01:09:10.150 --> 01:09:10.630
Yeah.

1477
01:09:12.350 --> 01:09:13.650
That's the one I like.

1478
01:09:13.730 --> 01:09:14.810
I just can't resist it.

1479
01:09:14.890 --> 01:09:19.670
When I see that, it's not everywhere, but when it's there, I grab one, you know.

1480
01:09:19.670 --> 01:09:23.770
But for food, it's tacos, you know.

1481
01:09:24.090 --> 01:09:27.410
I gotta say tacos with salsa and all that stuff.

1482
01:09:27.570 --> 01:09:28.390
I love tacos.

1483
01:09:28.730 --> 01:09:30.890
I also remember your dessert bar.

1484
01:09:31.090 --> 01:09:35.610
You talk about action stations, but one time you had like a make-your-own-sunday bar.

1485
01:09:36.130 --> 01:09:38.690
And it was like amazing.

1486
01:09:39.110 --> 01:09:39.330
Yeah.

1487
01:09:39.510 --> 01:09:41.590
And it was like one of the more summer months.

1488
01:09:41.730 --> 01:09:45.970
And I just remember how good that bowl of ice cream and I got to put all my toppings on it.

1489
01:09:46.210 --> 01:09:49.250
But was there a standout dessert that people loved?

1490
01:09:49.670 --> 01:09:50.810
The cookie cake.

1491
01:09:51.170 --> 01:09:51.730
Yes.

1492
01:09:51.850 --> 01:09:52.770
The hot cookie cake.

1493
01:09:53.050 --> 01:09:57.910
That one was a must every day, actually, with ice cream.

1494
01:09:58.610 --> 01:09:58.710
Yeah.

1495
01:09:58.790 --> 01:10:02.890
So it was on, you know, it's on a hot Schaefer.

1496
01:10:03.070 --> 01:10:05.530
So it's hot, nice and soft.

1497
01:10:05.750 --> 01:10:06.250
Oh, yeah.

1498
01:10:06.710 --> 01:10:07.010
Yeah.

1499
01:10:07.190 --> 01:10:08.350
That one's still a hit.

1500
01:10:08.590 --> 01:10:13.950
But that's the one that, for sure, because it wasn't there at the beginning.

1501
01:10:13.950 --> 01:10:16.990
It got there around, I think, season five or something.

1502
01:10:16.990 --> 01:10:21.450
So once it got there, it was, we couldn't take it out no more.

1503
01:10:21.750 --> 01:10:29.390
It had like this crusty, like I always wanted an edge piece because it would get nice and crispy around the edge.

1504
01:10:29.510 --> 01:10:31.830
And that was Steve's favorite dessert.

1505
01:10:32.050 --> 01:10:39.230
Steve and I would often meet at the warm chocolate chip cookie dish at the end of lunch.

1506
01:10:39.230 --> 01:10:40.610
And we would kind of laugh.

1507
01:10:40.750 --> 01:10:42.310
We'd be like, here we are again.

1508
01:10:42.330 --> 01:10:45.870
So we meet again over a warm chocolate chip cookie dessert.

1509
01:10:46.850 --> 01:10:48.190
I loved it.

1510
01:10:48.610 --> 01:10:49.110
Oh, yeah.

1511
01:10:49.290 --> 01:10:52.330
And also right there in stage three, right?

1512
01:10:54.350 --> 01:10:59.910
That was so special because all of the cast was, you know, Steve ate there.

1513
01:11:00.110 --> 01:11:01.230
Everybody ate there.

1514
01:11:01.410 --> 01:11:04.330
The crew and then decisions were made there.

1515
01:11:04.710 --> 01:11:06.810
Birthday parties celebrated there.

1516
01:11:07.170 --> 01:11:09.550
I mean, I love that stage.

1517
01:11:09.730 --> 01:11:11.250
And I'll never forget it.

1518
01:11:11.670 --> 01:11:11.910
You know?

1519
01:11:11.910 --> 01:11:18.690
Yeah, I loved it when they would, the stage was like, picture sort of for people listening, like a big aircraft hangar.

1520
01:11:18.810 --> 01:11:24.090
And they would open this giant door and then they would have these long tables.

1521
01:11:24.390 --> 01:11:27.990
And Sergio would be set up, you know, right outside that door.

1522
01:11:28.190 --> 01:11:31.230
And we'd be going through the food line and you'd have your food stations.

1523
01:11:31.470 --> 01:11:37.850
And there was this sort of open air, long tables, very communal kind of eating and gathering.

1524
01:11:37.850 --> 01:11:45.330
And you would see people from different departments, you know, you didn't feel isolated, like, oh, we just do this one thing and we don't interact.

1525
01:11:45.590 --> 01:11:52.390
Everybody was like mixing and mingling and talking and asking about each other's kids or, you know, do you have a trip planned?

1526
01:11:52.390 --> 01:11:56.810
And it was just a wonderful, big gathering every day.

1527
01:11:57.030 --> 01:12:05.410
It was also a great time to like meet crew members' families because families would come up during lunch and visit.

1528
01:12:05.410 --> 01:12:09.130
It was that way that like food brings you together, you know?

1529
01:12:09.390 --> 01:12:09.950
Yes.

1530
01:12:10.150 --> 01:12:12.590
And it doesn't happen anymore like that in any crew.

1531
01:12:12.770 --> 01:12:14.050
I mean, it really doesn't.

1532
01:12:14.190 --> 01:12:20.570
You know, the people in their trailers now and, you know, it doesn't happen anymore.

1533
01:12:20.770 --> 01:12:27.050
I mean, where everybody, the writers, everybody there, it's just mingling.

1534
01:12:27.350 --> 01:12:33.390
That's my favorite moment there at stage three, you know, it's just seeing everybody there.

1535
01:12:33.390 --> 01:12:34.250
That's right.

1536
01:12:34.750 --> 01:12:37.830
You know, family members, kids, all that stuff.

1537
01:12:38.430 --> 01:12:38.950
Yeah.

1538
01:12:39.590 --> 01:12:40.230
It was cool.

1539
01:12:40.550 --> 01:12:45.030
I think I didn't realize how special that was till I went to work on other projects.

1540
01:12:45.030 --> 01:12:48.170
And it is sort of like people just kind of grab their food and go.

1541
01:12:48.490 --> 01:12:48.930
Yeah.

1542
01:12:49.290 --> 01:12:51.090
I'm so thankful we had that.

1543
01:12:51.230 --> 01:12:54.250
It kind of felt like Thanksgiving gathering every day.

1544
01:12:54.510 --> 01:12:54.970
Every day.

1545
01:12:55.130 --> 01:12:55.830
It did.

1546
01:12:56.430 --> 01:12:56.890
Yes.

1547
01:12:57.490 --> 01:12:59.330
Sergio, this was so wonderful.

1548
01:12:59.810 --> 01:13:00.190
Yeah.

1549
01:13:00.470 --> 01:13:01.010
It's awesome.

1550
01:13:01.410 --> 01:13:02.450
Sorry, I'm a little nervous.

1551
01:13:02.450 --> 01:13:03.090
But yeah.

1552
01:13:03.650 --> 01:13:05.050
Oh, you're doing great.

1553
01:13:05.270 --> 01:13:05.710
Thank you.

1554
01:13:05.810 --> 01:13:05.950
Thank you.

1555
01:13:05.950 --> 01:13:07.270
You didn't seem nervous at all.

1556
01:13:07.470 --> 01:13:08.510
No, not at all.

1557
01:13:08.870 --> 01:13:10.810
Was there anything we missed, Sergio?

1558
01:13:10.990 --> 01:13:12.970
Anything you want to share that we didn't cover?

1559
01:13:13.750 --> 01:13:16.010
It's nice going back to memory lane.

1560
01:13:16.190 --> 01:13:22.970
And, you know, like last night I saw the last episode and I cried, you know, like because we

1561
01:13:22.970 --> 01:13:27.010
were talking about it and I said, let me watch the last episode.

1562
01:13:27.010 --> 01:13:29.790
So, like, you know, last night I haven't watched it in a minute.

1563
01:13:30.190 --> 01:13:35.770
It was nice, you know, because it was so real, you know, like the real reactions, everything.

1564
01:13:36.410 --> 01:13:37.750
I just saw it last night.

1565
01:13:37.890 --> 01:13:38.210
That's what.

1566
01:13:38.650 --> 01:13:42.030
And so, you know, it's nice to come back to memory lane.

1567
01:13:42.550 --> 01:13:44.990
Would you watch the show when it was on, Sergio?

1568
01:13:45.230 --> 01:13:46.610
Did you guys watch it each week?

1569
01:13:46.610 --> 01:13:53.230
I started watching it around season three and then, yeah, during when we were working.

1570
01:13:53.670 --> 01:13:59.670
And then I'm about to do a rewatch to go with you as soon because seeing yesterday's

1571
01:13:59.670 --> 01:14:04.110
episode made me want to, you know what, I'm going to start this up again, you know.

1572
01:14:04.290 --> 01:14:05.090
I owe them all.

1573
01:14:05.290 --> 01:14:05.650
Yeah.

1574
01:14:06.070 --> 01:14:08.170
It'd be nice and doing that through the office ladies.

1575
01:14:08.750 --> 01:14:09.150
It'd be awesome.

1576
01:14:09.290 --> 01:14:10.690
Aw, thanks, Sergio.

1577
01:14:11.150 --> 01:14:11.490
Yeah.

1578
01:14:11.690 --> 01:14:13.930
We've really loved rewatching the show.

1579
01:14:14.130 --> 01:14:15.510
It's been so much fun.

1580
01:14:15.510 --> 01:14:21.630
And plus, just the joy of us getting to reach out and reconnect with so many people who are

1581
01:14:21.630 --> 01:14:22.890
so special to us, like you.

1582
01:14:23.530 --> 01:14:24.270
Oh, thank you.

1583
01:14:24.590 --> 01:14:24.890
Thank you.

1584
01:14:24.990 --> 01:14:26.190
You're special to me, too.

1585
01:14:26.630 --> 01:14:28.210
Everybody is on the office.

1586
01:14:28.350 --> 01:14:29.550
Aw, thank you, Sergio.

1587
01:14:29.670 --> 01:14:30.190
Love you.

1588
01:14:30.430 --> 01:14:30.990
Thank you.

1589
01:14:31.370 --> 01:14:32.490
Thank you so much.

1590
01:14:32.690 --> 01:14:33.250
Love you, too.

1591
01:14:36.590 --> 01:14:41.910
I think you can just hear in Sergio's voice how special the office was to him and cooking

1592
01:14:41.910 --> 01:14:43.450
and caring for people.

1593
01:14:43.770 --> 01:14:45.070
Yeah, we were such a community.

1594
01:14:45.070 --> 01:14:45.630
Yeah.

1595
01:14:45.670 --> 01:14:50.510
When the three of us were talking, I feel like you can see how there were not these

1596
01:14:50.510 --> 01:14:52.770
like distinct cliques of people.

1597
01:14:52.970 --> 01:14:54.410
We all blended together.

1598
01:14:54.770 --> 01:14:55.030
Yeah.

1599
01:14:55.450 --> 01:15:00.890
